// SwiftStats.xcconfig — analytics write-key injection for the `scarf` app target.
//
// The swift-stats write key must never be committed. It reaches the app as:
//
//     SwiftStatsLocal.xcconfig  →  SWIFT_STATS_WRITE_KEY (build setting)
//                               →  SwiftStatsWriteKey (Info.plist)
//                               →  read at runtime by Analytics.swift
//
// `SwiftStatsLocal.xcconfig` is an UNCOMMITTED sibling of this file
// (gitignored) that a developer or a CI step creates with a single line:
//
//     SWIFT_STATS_WRITE_KEY = sk_stats_…
//
// Order matters: the empty default is declared FIRST and the optional include
// comes after, so a local definition overrides it. The include is optional
// (`#include?`), so a fresh checkout without that file still builds — the key
// stays empty and the app degrades to no-op analytics at runtime.
//
// Rotation happens in the ScarfMon dashboard; no key ever lands in git.

SWIFT_STATS_WRITE_KEY =

#include? "SwiftStatsLocal.xcconfig"
